re expected to take part in the Indian opposition's planned mega march in New Delhi over a controversial revision of electoral rolls. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Trump grants visa to mother of Ghanaian boy killed in NYC — Mamdani</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bbce5be5ef05de82b193b3ebdcce68607a459585e8fdb10150016982df9cb193</id><updated>2026-11-01T06:27:51Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T03:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-grants-visa-to-mother-of-ghanaian-boy-killed-in-nyc-mamdani/a-79820019--ed613f7f7bb0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-grants-visa-to-mother-of-ghanaian-boy-killed-in-nyc-mamdani/a-79820019?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Javits Frimpong was on his way to school when he was shot in a neighborhood in the Bronx. He was 15 years old.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>FBI says North Korea behind $6 billion Binance crypto theft</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ef0d5c7b0c35222e092d8c0b9a7e8572a5e610c7e1ae1be101c65583f60b2980</id><updated>2026-11-01T06:27:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-01T01:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fbi-says-north-korea-behind-6-billion-binance-crypto-theft/a-79819998--ddc7ca6650b8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fbi-says-north-korea-behind-6-billion-binance-crypto-theft/a-79819998?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The FBI said the theft was tied to "malicious cyber activity" by an entity known as TraderTraitor, the same actors behind a $1.5 billion Bybit hack last year.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Serbia after Vucic: The winners are losing patience</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c9803223e61abb39d32d569e4e3e814163f20d0f336a428ab6a5004e83b3286e</id><updated>2026-11-01T06:26:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T19:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/serbia-after-vucic-the-winners-are-losing-patience/a-79817586--7cebe42bf331.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/serbia-after-vucic-the-winners-are-losing-patience/a-79817586?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After the Student List's election victory, Aleksandar Vucic's power apparatus is disintegrating. People want justice as soon as possible. But the losers still hold sway in the judiciary and administration.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>More than 290 arrested in France as some weekend protests turn violent</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5baf97c428fa83867710621904e49ea62e1a41163c89f07e5a3225fc1f77884e</id><updated>2026-11-01T06:26:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T18:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/more-than-290-arrested-in-france-as-some-weekend-protests-turn-violent/a-79818138--cf89bc00ce66.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/more-than-290-arrested-in-france-as-some-weekend-protests-turn-violent/a-79818138?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Protests continue across France as 320,000 people take to the streets over rising living costs and poor school conditions for a third consecutive weekend, with clashes reported in several cities.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's Gen Z protests disrupted by violence on Saturday</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:75c196ac4810ed838a7a37433e4ede9730e2ae1846bcc19735501ff4cb461ec2</id><updated>2026-11-01T06:27:57Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T16:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-gen-z-protests-disrupted-by-violence-on-saturday/live-79814694--76fbedb708ba.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-gen-z-protests-disrupted-by-violence-on-saturday/live-79814694?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nationwide protests led by young people were largely peaceful throughout the day, but reports about looting and rioting in the evening, especially in Frankfurt, overshadowed the spirit of the demonstrations.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine news: Evacuees from Russian-occupied Oleshky reach Kyiv-controlled territory</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9c2dd4332e6c841d8ec640eebecad5a450752a8302d5c46ca105e234f712a542</id><updated>2026-11-01T06:26:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T15:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-news-evacuees-from-russian-occupied-oleshky-reach-kyiv-controlled-territory/live-79815409--dd2b30369e3a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-news-evacuees-from-russian-occupied-oleshky-reach-kyiv-controlled-territory/live-79815409?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After Melania Trump reportedly brokered a localized truce, residents of Ukraine's Oleshky managed to leave the occupied city. Meanwhile, Kyiv claimed a hit on a Russian rocket fuel plant. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Merkel calls for first female president</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2ccf539311345cd9696a051f0e9226158bd57b65c76ebcd2180e4984392cbb26</id><updated>2026-11-01T06:26:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T11:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merkel-calls-for-first-female-president/live-79814961--0935202de27a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-merkel-calls-for-first-female-president/live-79814961?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Former Chancellor Angela Merkel says it's time to consider a woman as Germany's next president. Meanwhile, Berlin's Left Party is deciding whether to enter coalition talks. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Bollywood and the underworld — together in the spotlight?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b1dc695ad293543027719d16f0f98846cd2ab1f37c3e64a7db822b478ac38e37</id><updated>2026-11-01T06:26:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T07:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bollywood-and-the-underworld-together-in-the-spotlight/a-79806129--e6b957cc58ac.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bollywood-and-the-underworld-together-in-the-spotlight/a-79806129?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A wave of shootings and extortion threats has rattled India's film industry. This time, those claiming responsibility are very different from the Mumbai underworld that had Bollywood in its grip back in the 1990s.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Embarrassing name? How we live with names we don't like</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7832882226a0338807110f34aaa0ae9f6e60e69445c2e54e84585e11cfd4fae5</id><updated>2026-11-01T06:26:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T05:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/embarrassing-name-how-we-live-with-names-we-don-t-like/a-79724068--afb6ee0b7720.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/embarrassing-name-how-we-live-with-names-we-don-t-like/a-79724068?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">What happens when your name evokes laughter or ridicule? Research points to negative life outcomes, but some people learn to embrace unfortunate names.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Amit Shah challenges Rahul Gandhi to debate vote theft in parliament</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6f72191810d2a7270c85c82611c2dca5c4331980ee06f616396caecc06ff500e</id><updated>2026-11-01T06:26:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T05:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-amit-shah-challenges-rahul-gandhi-to-debate-vote-theft-in-parliament/live-79814329--39045e872cba.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-amit-shah-challenges-rahul-gandhi-to-debate-vote-theft-in-parliament/live-79814329?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Home Minister Amit Shah has challenged Rahul Gandhi to debate electoral irregularity allegations in parliament, ahead of a major opposition rally against the election chief in Delhi.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>UN peacekeeping mission in Western Sahara to expire amid US, Russia vetoes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2fd117b84052102617f16425aa54e4a2d2eeb24e2be04cfe714af0bf33aa458d</id><updated>2026-11-01T06:26:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T04:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/un-peacekeeping-mission-in-western-sahara-to-expire-amid-us-russia-vetoes/a-79814338--f1640d90bbfc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/un-peacekeeping-mission-in-western-sahara-to-expire-amid-us-russia-vetoes/a-79814338?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The mandate of the UN peacekeeping force in Western Sahara will expire on October 31. The UN Security Council could not agree on a resolution to extend the mission.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>European diplomats shun Russia at G20 gathering in the US</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2892aef3eb3fd0f831c03ddc8d688ef88b4bb74d20ee8e848f69d74ff7a6822b</id><updated>2026-11-01T06:26:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-31T01:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/european-diplomats-shun-russia-at-g20-gathering-in-the-us/a-79813925--30998c0899d1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/european-diplomats-shun-russia-at-g20-gathering-in-the-us/a-79813925?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russian Foreign Minister Sergey Lavrov declined to comment on Russia's participation in the G20 summit in December, telling DW that Volodymyr Zelenskyy should travel to Russia if he wanted talks with Vladimir Putin.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Poland: Protesters, police clash amid top court standoff</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:90d5fd34a1bc4d20379e2c459883e27c6357ee71e4cfc20054e3fa786fee7b43</id><updated>2026-11-01T06:26:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T23:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/poland-protesters-police-clash-amid-top-court-standoff/a-79813882--7486d7cd78e0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/poland-protesters-police-clash-amid-top-court-standoff/a-79813882?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Polish Prime Minister Donald Tusk defended the suspension of top court President Bogdan Swieczkowski as a move to "restore the rule of law."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Canadian PM Mark Carney discusses talks with the EU, overdependence on the US and how to deal with Donald Trump in a DW interview.</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:27a405bc41cb603ec2c9ea33835b50c8497955d940006f4cdf0917b074d27fcc</id><updated>2026-11-01T06:26:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T20:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/canadian-pm-mark-carney-discusses-talks-with-the-eu-overdependence-on-the-us-and-how-to-deal-with-do/a-79811469--a55bfac7d94c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/canadian-pm-mark-carney-discusses-talks-with-the-eu-overdependence-on-the-us-and-how-to-deal-with-donald-trump-in-a-dw-interview/a-79811469?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Prime Minister Mark Carney tells DW that Canada is seeking closer EU ties to "diversify and deepen" partnerships beyond the Americas. Despite German pushback, he said he favors the all-new term "associate membership."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: Oleshky residents evacuate war-ravaged city</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:39ba6c1fc476bbeeec01084640b4a12405145e1d4b501d93d5fae3c8f419615d</id><updated>2026-11-01T06:26:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T20:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-oleshky-residents-evacuate-war-ravaged-city/a-79812327--58d4dbca74c5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-oleshky-residents-evacuate-war-ravaged-city/a-79812327?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Under the local ceasefire, an aid convoy of 25 buses arrived with humanitarian aid and as transport for fleeing Oleshky residents. The Ukrainian city has been occupied by Russia since 2022 and faces food shortages.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Smuggling, power, profit: Irregular migration out of eastern Libya</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4adcfe7e3e9636610be0c5d11f297255bf8502df211d6607ef52686fbe3840b6</id><updated>2026-11-01T06:26:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T18:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/irregular-migration-from-libya-to-crete-is-rising-raising-questions-about-the-links-between-people-s/a-79808822--583a8979ee7e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/smuggling-power-profit-irregular-migration-out-of-eastern-libya/a-79808822?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">There is currently more irregular migration between eastern Libya and Crete, Greece. It's raising questions as to what connects people smugglers with powerful militias in eastern Libya and then in turn, Europeans.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Tennessee woman Christa Pike describes pain after failed execution</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cdfecaf51c20c6bd544b1f8e2fd17941834dd611b113cd05ebf377c52a774328</id><updated>2026-11-01T06:26:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T16:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tennessee-woman-christa-pike-describes-pain-after-failed-execution/a-79810735--d4af8b5b3af1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tennessee-woman-christa-pike-describes-pain-after-failed-execution/a-79810735?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Christa Pike says she remains in constant pain a month after surviving a lethal injection in Tennessee. Her lawyers want her death sentence reduced to life, while the state governor has ordered an investigation.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>What the rift within the Tsikhanouski family means for the Belarusian opposition in exile</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:428d8e1ae83a4b7bef9f4b5549f5c64b8743dd796073b1e8e1e04e5ea0ce02e6</id><updated>2026-11-01T06:26:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T16:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-the-rift-within-the-tsikhanouski-family-means-for-the-belarusian-opposition-in-exile/a-79802776--7fdd2527b18a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-the-rift-within-the-tsikhanouski-family-means-for-the-belarusian-opposition-in-exile/a-79802776?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Siarhei Tsikhanouski criticizes the work of his wife, Sviatlana Tsikhanouskaya, and her office. He also questions her legitimacy. What are the implications for Belarusian political forces in exile?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>US midterms: Pope Leo XIV casts vote by mail</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e0f1ac6c90a846cbafe2293d05964c81556eade56a919129d9c3160dbb5ef688</id><updated>2026-11-01T06:26:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-30T16:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-midterms-pope-leo-xiv-casts-vote-by-mail/a-79810339--3e151727f070.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-midterms-pope-leo-xiv-casts-vote-by-mail/a-79810339?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As a US citizen, Pope Leo XIV is eligible to vote in US elections and has made use of that right with a postal ballot ahead of Tuesday's midterms. The pontiff, a Chicago native, did not reveal who he voted for.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
